<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Designing for Restoration Not Extraction — Madeleine Smith</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Crimson+Pro:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #EDE4F3;          /* lavender — matches homepage page bg */
    --surface: #FAF7F2;     /* cream — for cream text on dark cards */
    --bg-soft: #E8E0D4;     /* parchment — warm neutral surface */
    --bg-card: #D5CAE0;     /* lavender divider tone */
    --ink: #3D2E52;         /* dark plum — matches homepage --text */
    --ink-soft: #6B5A80;    /* muted plum — matches homepage --text-muted */
    --ink-faint: #6B5A80;   /* same as ink-soft for readability on lavender */
    --teal: #4A7C8A;        /* pacific teal — matches homepage --accent-pacific */
    --teal-deep: #3D6373;
    --rust: #9E6B5A;        /* terracotta — matches homepage --accent-terracotta */
    --plum: #574A66;        /* deep plum — fits lavender family */
    --plum-deep: #4A3D5C;
    --rule: #E0D5C9;        /* matches homepage --border */
    --rule-faint: #D5CAE0;  /* matches homepage --divider */
    --slate: #5C6B73;       /* matches homepage --body */

    --serif: 'Crimson Pro', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
    --sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;

    --content-max: 680px;
    --shell-max: 1100px;    /* matches homepage container */
  }

  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }

  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-feature-settings: "ss01", "kern";
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
  }

  ::selection { background: var(--rust); color: var(--surface); }

  /* ----------- LAYOUT ----------- */
  .shell {
    max-width: var(--shell-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 56px 48px 60px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 64px;
  }

  header.top {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--teal);
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 7px 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--teal);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: transparent;
    transition: color 220ms ease, background 220ms ease, border-color 220ms ease;
  }
  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--bg);
    background: var(--teal);
    border-color: var(--teal);
  }

  /* ----------- SIDEBAR NAV ----------- */
  .sidenav {
    position: sticky;
    top: 56px;
    align-self: start;
    padding-top: 8px;
  }

  .sidenav ol {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .sidenav li {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .sidenav a {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--slate);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 240ms ease;
    padding: 4px 0;
  }

  .sidenav a::before {
    content: '';
    width: 18px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--slate);
    transition: width 240ms ease, background 240ms ease;
  }

  .sidenav a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  .sidenav a:hover::before { background: var(--ink); }

  .sidenav a.active {
    color: var(--rust);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .sidenav a.active::before {
    width: 28px;
    height: 1.5px;
    background: var(--rust);
  }

  /* ----------- ARTICLE ----------- */
  article {
    max-width: var(--content-max);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rust);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 420;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 144, "SOFT" 30;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 5.5vw, 64px);
    line-height: 1.04;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--teal);
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }

  .subtitle {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 40px;
    max-width: 580px;
  }

  .byline {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0 0 48px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--rust);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 44px 0 32px;
  }

  h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 460;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 60, "SOFT" 30;
    font-size: 28px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--teal);
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  p em, .pullquote {
    font-style: italic;
  }

  a.inline {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    transition: border-color 220ms ease;
  }
  a.inline:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--rust); }

  /* ----------- STAT GRID ----------- */
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 48px 0 56px;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  .stat {
    background: var(--plum);
    color: var(--surface);
    padding: 36px 32px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    min-height: 180px;
  }

  .stat.tall {
    grid-row: span 2;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .stat.tall .stat-figure {
    font-size: clamp(96px, 13vw, 160px);
  }
  .stat.small { min-height: 0; padding: 24px 28px; }

  .stat-figure {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 144, "SOFT" 50;
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: clamp(48px, 6vw, 72px);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .stat.small .stat-figure {
    font-size: clamp(36px, 4vw, 48px);
  }

  .stat-label {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    opacity: 0.88;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  /* ----------- METHOD EXPLORER ----------- */
  .tier-intro {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .tier-explorer {
    margin: 16px 0 56px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .tier-card {
    color: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: relative;
  }

  .tier-1 { background: var(--rust); }
  .tier-2 { background: var(--teal); }
  .tier-3 { background: var(--plum); }

  .tier-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 28px;
    padding: 26px 32px;
    cursor: pointer;
    user-select: none;
    border: none;
    background: transparent;
    width: 100%;
    text-align: left;
    font-family: inherit;
    color: inherit;
  }

  .tier-num {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--surface);
    opacity: 0.65;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .tier-name {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 460;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 36, "SOFT" 30;
    font-size: 24px;
    color: var(--surface);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .tier-name .descriptor {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--surface);
    opacity: 0.78;
    margin-top: 4px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
  }

  .tier-toggle {
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid rgba(250, 247, 242, 0.4);
    background: transparent;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    transition: transform 320ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1), border-color 240ms ease;
    color: var(--surface);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .tier-card.open .tier-toggle {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    border-color: var(--surface);
  }

  .tier-toggle svg { width: 12px; height: 12px; }

  .tier-body {
    max-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: max-height 480ms cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
  }

  .tier-card.open .tier-body {
    max-height: 800px;
  }

  .tier-body-inner {
    padding: 4px 40px 36px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 32px 40px;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(250, 247, 242, 0.18);
    padding-top: 28px;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .tier-field {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .tier-field.full {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .tier-field-label {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--surface);
    opacity: 0.7;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .tier-field-body {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--surface);
  }

  /* ----------- MAPPING TABLE ----------- */
  .mapping {
    background: var(--bg-soft);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 32px 36px;
    margin: 32px 0 48px;
    max-width: 700px;
  }

  .mapping-header {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
    padding-bottom: 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .mapping-header span {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .mapping-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .mapping-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .mapping-row .from {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .mapping-row .to {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 17px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 420;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  /* ----------- CLOSING ----------- */
  .closing {
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding-top: 56px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .closing p {
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .closing .first-letter {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 144, "SOFT" 50;
    font-weight: 380;
    font-size: 56px;
    line-height: 0.9;
    color: var(--rust);
    float: left;
    margin: 6px 10px -4px 0;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .closing .cta {
    margin-top: 44px;
    padding-top: 44px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* ----------- FOOTER ----------- */
  footer {
    grid-column: 2 / -1;
    margin-top: 60px;
    padding-top: 40px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    max-width: var(--content-max);
  }

  footer p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  /* ----------- MOBILE ----------- */
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .shell {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
      padding: 32px 24px 40px;
    }
    .sidenav { display: none; }
    header.top { margin-bottom: 28px; }
    .byline { margin-bottom: 32px; }
    h2 { margin: 32px 0 24px; }

    .stats { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .stat.tall { grid-row: auto; }

    .tier-head {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
      gap: 16px;
      padding: 22px 24px;
    }
    .tier-num { display: none; }
    .tier-body-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 24px;
      padding: 28px 28px 32px;
    }

    .mapping-row, .mapping-header { gap: 16px; }

    footer {
      grid-column: 1;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 12px;
    }
  }

  /* ----------- ENTRANCE ANIMATION ----------- */
  .fade-in {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(8px);
    animation: fadeIn 800ms cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.6, 0.2, 1) forwards;
  }
  .fade-in:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: 0ms; }
  .fade-in:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 80ms; }
  .fade-in:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 160ms; }
  .fade-in:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: 240ms; }

  @keyframes fadeIn {
    to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="shell">

  <header class="top">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to home</a>
  </header>

  <nav class="sidenav" aria-label="Section navigation">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#question" data-target="question">The Question</a></li>
      <li><a href="#method" data-target="method">The Method</a></li>
      <li><a href="#heard" data-target="heard">What We Heard</a></li>
      <li><a href="#mapping" data-target="mapping">Where It Maps</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <article>

      <div class="fade-in">
        <div class="eyebrow">Case Study · UX Research</div>
      </div>

      <h1 class="fade-in">Designing for Restoration Not Extraction</h1>

      <p class="subtitle fade-in">A formative qualitative study with seven program sites, conducted before the system that would serve them was designed.</p>

      <p class="byline fade-in">Madeleine Smith &nbsp;·&nbsp; 2025</p>

      <!-- QUESTION -->
      <section id="question">
        <h2>The Question</h2>

        <p>Before building a centralized data system for a 150-person youth-serving nonprofit, I wanted to know what the people who would actually use it were already doing. Not in the abstract. In their daily workflows, at their specific sites, on the actual mornings they ran intake.</p>

        <p>The org's instinct was to design the system first and roll it out second. The risk in that sequence is well-known: tools land on workflows they don't understand, staff route around the system, the system becomes a reporting requirement instead of a daily tool, and the data it captures stops mapping to reality. The research below was the work I ran to keep that from happening.</p>

        <p>I designed a formative qualitative study — seven in-depth interviews, one team per school site, deliberately scoped to listen before designing. The goal was discovery, not validation. I didn't bring a prototype. I brought questions.</p>

        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat tall">
            <div class="stat-figure">7</div>
            <div class="stat-label">School sites covered, with site leaders and assistant leaders interviewed as teams of 2–4.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat small">
            <div class="stat-figure">60 min</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Per interview, semi-structured, walkthrough format.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="stat small">
            <div class="stat-figure">15+</div>
            <div class="stat-label">Parent codes surfaced through thematic analysis, with 4–5 child codes each.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- METHOD -->
      <section id="method">
        <h2>The Method</h2>

        <h3>Semi-structured interviews, AI-assisted thematic analysis, researcher review at every layer.</h3>

        <p class="tier-intro">The method was designed to surface what existed already — workflows, workarounds, pain points, the systems sites had quietly built for themselves — rather than to test what was being planned. Three components, each doing distinct work.</p>

        <p class="tier-intro">The full study took four months in a nonprofit setting. The same study in a SaaS or product environment would run in roughly two weeks. The difference isn't methodological. It's that I ran this study solo, as one of many concurrent priorities, in an org without dedicated research infrastructure. In a product environment with a research function, scheduling, transcription, and synthesis support compress that timeline by an order of magnitude.</p>

        <div class="tier-explorer">

          <!-- METHOD 1: Protocol design -->
          <article class="tier-card tier-1" data-tier="1">
            <button class="tier-head" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tier-1-body">
              <span class="tier-num">Method 01</span>
              <span class="tier-name">Protocol design
                <span class="descriptor">Discovery interviews</span>
              </span>
              <span class="tier-toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                  <path d="M6 1V11M1 6H11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
            </button>
            <div class="tier-body" id="tier-1-body">
              <div class="tier-body-inner">
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">What I asked</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">Walk me through a typical day. What changes by season. How data moves through your workflow, end to end. Where it breaks. The hours each task actually takes. What you've built locally to compensate for what doesn't work.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Format</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">Semi-structured, 60-minute interviews with site teams of 2–4 — site leaders and assistant leaders together — so workflow descriptions could be cross-checked in real time.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">The open close</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">Every interview ended with an open invitation to add anything else. Most participants used that space to surface system-level grievances they hadn't been asked about directly — which became some of the highest-signal data in the study.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Why it mattered</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">The protocol was built to find what I didn't know to ask about. Walkthroughs surface workflows; open closes surface beliefs. The combination is what makes formative research formative.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- METHOD 2: AI-assisted thematic analysis -->
          <article class="tier-card tier-2" data-tier="2">
            <button class="tier-head" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tier-2-body">
              <span class="tier-num">Method 02</span>
              <span class="tier-name">AI-assisted thematic analysis
                <span class="descriptor">Coding &amp; synthesis</span>
              </span>
              <span class="tier-toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                  <path d="M6 1V11M1 6H11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
            </button>
            <div class="tier-body" id="tier-2-body">
              <div class="tier-body-inner">
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">The starting frame</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">I coded the first 12 parent codes manually, based on the protocol's question architecture and what emerged in the first two interview transcripts.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Where Claude entered</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">I gave Claude the 12 codes and asked it to apply them across the full transcript set as a first pass, surfacing where codes applied, where they didn't fit, and where new themes were emerging.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Researcher review</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">I worked through Claude's output line by line. Where I agreed, the code held. Where I disagreed, I revised. Where Claude surfaced a theme I hadn't seen, I assessed it against the full transcript and either adopted, refined, or rejected it. The final code structure landed at roughly 15 parent codes with 4–5 child codes each.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Why it mattered</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">AI-assisted coding compresses synthesis time without sacrificing researcher judgment — provided the researcher reviews every output. The method is faster than manual coding and more rigorous than AI alone.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- METHOD 3: Findings & recommendations -->
          <article class="tier-card tier-3" data-tier="3">
            <button class="tier-head" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="tier-3-body">
              <span class="tier-num">Method 03</span>
              <span class="tier-name">Findings &amp; recommendations
                <span class="descriptor">Deliverable</span>
              </span>
              <span class="tier-toggle" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                  <path d="M6 1V11M1 6H11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
                </svg>
              </span>
            </button>
            <div class="tier-body" id="tier-3-body">
              <div class="tier-body-inner">
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">What I produced</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">A key findings and recommendations report for the executive director, structured around the themes that emerged and the workflow shifts those themes pointed to.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Audience</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">Executive leadership. The report was designed to surface what the research changed about how the system should be designed — not to validate decisions already made.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Recommendation shape</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">The recommendation was a sequencing call: pause new quantitative metric expansion, prioritize Salesforce adoption and staff onboarding, allow iterative adjustment of the existing system, and route qualitative material to the revenue-generating department (development) in the interim. Primary and secondary data analysis showed the org had 18–24 months of qualitative runway before quantitative expansion was warranted. The evidence didn't support asking site staff to carry more measurement work; it supported consolidating what existed.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="tier-field">
                  <span class="tier-field-label">Why it mattered</span>
                  <p class="tier-field-body">Recommendations rooted in seven workflow walkthroughs hold up better than recommendations rooted in assumptions. The deliverable was meant to be the foundation of the next phase of evaluation framework design.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- HEARD -->
      <section id="heard">
        <h2>What We Heard</h2>

        <h3>The patterns the interviews surfaced.</h3>

        <p>The dominant finding was the gap between the org's stated data ambitions and the workflow reality at the sites. Site teams were already running on tight margins, building local workarounds — spreadsheets, paper trackers, side conversations with school administrators — to keep their programs viable. The systems they'd quietly constructed weren't gaps to fill with more tooling. They were evidence of what the central system would need to honor.</p>

        <p>MGMT and school administration emerged as the most common pain points across sites, surfacing in nearly every interview through the open-close prompt. Site staff didn't volunteer those grievances when asked about workflows directly. They surfaced them when invited to add anything else — which made the open close the single most generative protocol decision in the study.</p>

        <p>The research challenged the org's working assumption that more metrics would produce better evaluation. Primary and secondary data analysis showed the opposite: the existing qualitative material was underutilized, and the revenue-generating department could draw more value from what already existed than from anything new the sites might produce. The recommendation that followed wasn't to slow down. It was to sequence — adoption first, qualitative consolidation second, quantitative expansion deferred.</p>
      </section>

      <!-- MAPPING -->
      <section id="mapping">
        <h2>Where It Maps</h2>

        <h3>The work was discovery research, framed as evaluation.</h3>

        <p>Discovery research and formative evaluation share a methodological core: structured listening before structured intervention. The vocabulary differs by industry, but the work runs on the same logic.</p>

        <div class="mapping">
          <div class="mapping-header">
            <span>What it was in the role</span>
            <span>What it maps to</span>
          </div>

          <div class="mapping-row">
            <div class="from">Semi-structured 60-min interviews with end users</div>
